          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            A 2 lb tub of Aldi's Elevation whey holds roughly 18 to 21 servings and a 24 oz tub roughly 14 to 15, each with 30 g of protein per the label at the time of writing. At one shake a day that is about three weeks from the big tub and two from the small one. The net weight on the front of the tub tells you which you have, and the serving description on the back tells you whether a serving is one scoop or two.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            If both sizes are on the shelf, the 2 lb tub is the better buy. Either way, count your protein in servings and days, size your purchase to your Aldi trips, and use a shake to fill the gap between your meals and your target rather than as a goal in itself.
